{
  "title": "Triceps Rupture",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/shoulder-and-elbow/3071/triceps-rupture",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jan 24 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Triceps Ruptures are rare injuries to the elbow extensor mechanism that most commonly occurs as a result of a sudden forceful elbow contraction in weightlifters or older males with underlying systemic illness.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis can be made clinically with the inability to extend the elbow against resistance. MRI studies can help discern between partial and complete tears.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is either immobilization or primary repair depending on patient age, patient underlying systemic disease, chronicity of injury and patient activity demands.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "accounts for 0.8% of tendon ruptures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "more common in males 2:1",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "age 30-50 most common",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "commonly seen in",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "competitive weightlifting",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "body building",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "football players",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Risk factors",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**systemic illness** (hyperparathyroidism, renal osteodystrophy, OI, RA, type I DM)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**anabolic steroid use**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**local steroid injection**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**fluoroquinolone use**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "chronic olecranon bursitis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "previous triceps surgery",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Marfan syndrome",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "mechanism of injury",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "results from forceful eccentric contraction or FOOSH",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "pathoantomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "rupture most commonly occurs at the osseous insertion of the medial or lateral head",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "less frequently occurs through the muscle belly or at the musculotendinous junction",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Triceps brachii",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pennate muscle comprised of 3 heads",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3071/images/triceps.001..jpg",
                  "caption": "triceps anatomy"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "lateral",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "originates from the posterior humerus between the insertion of the teres minor and the superior aspect of spiral groove, the lateral border of humerus, and the lateral intermuscular septum",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "long",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "originates from the infraglenoid tuberosity",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "medial",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "originates from the posterior humerus distal to spiral groove, the medial humerus, and the medial intermuscular septum",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "insertion occurs over a wide area/footprint",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "inserts on average **1.1 cm distal to the tip of the olecranon**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "width ranges from 1.9-4.2cm",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "consists of",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "triceps tendon proper",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "confluence of tendon from all three heads",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "3",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "inserts on the olecranon",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "3",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "lateral triceps expansion",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "medial aspect inserts on the posterior crest of the ulna, adjacent to the medial head",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "3",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "lateral aspect inserts on the fascia of the extensor carpi ulnaris muscle and the deep fascia of the anconeus muscle",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "3",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "distal aspect inserts on the antebrachial fascia",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "3",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "only muscle in the posterior compartment of the arm",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "innervated by radial nerve (C6-C8)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Classification",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "No formal classification system exists",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Can describe the characteristics of the rupture",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "degree of tear",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "complete",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "partial",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "intact",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "location of tear",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "muscle belly",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "musculotendinous junction",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "tendinous insertion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "avulsion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "integrity of lateral expansion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "intact",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "torn",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "History",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "patients often note a painful pop",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "inspection",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "pain, swelling, and ecchymosis over the posterior aspect of the elbow",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**may have palpable defect**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "motion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**inability to extend elbow against resistance**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**not always present -- some patients are able to extend elbow against resistance if intact lateral expansion or compensating anconeus muscle**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "provocative tests",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "modified Thompson squeeze test",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**patient lies prone with the elbow at the end of the table and forearm hanging down**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**triceps muscle is firmly squeezed**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**inability to extend the elbow against gravity suggests complete disruption of triceps proper and lateral expansion**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "lateral",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**may show \"flake sign\" on lateral view**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3071/images/picture1.jpg",
                      "caption": "Elbow lateral"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "useful for determining location and severity",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3071/images/picture2.jpg",
                      "caption": "Sag image of the elbow"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**partial rupture**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**small fluid-filled defect within distal triceps tendon**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**complete rupture**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**large fluid-filled gap (paratricipital edema)**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Non-operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "splint immobilization",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "partial tears and able to extend against gravity",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "low demand patients in poor health",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "techniques",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "immobilize elbow in 30 degrees of flexion for 4 weeks",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "primary surgical repair",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "acute complete tears",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "partial tears (>50%) with significant weakness",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "transosseous tunnels",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "suture anchor",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "studies have shown **no difference in biomechanical strength or functional outcomes between transosseous bone tunnels and suture anchors**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "-1",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "**higher re-rupture rate and complication rate** noted with transosseous repair compared to suture anchor repair",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "-1",
                              "children": []
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "delayed reconstruction may need tendon graft",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Techniques",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Primary surgical repair**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "approach",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "posterolateral approach",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "techniques",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "based of location of tear",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "myotendinous junction",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "V-Y triceps tendon advancement",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "can augment using plantaris tendon",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "tendinous insertion",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "Bunnell or Krackow whipstitch technique using non-absorbable sutures secured via",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "transosseous tunnels",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "2",
                              "children": []
                            },
                            {
                              "text": "direct repair to periosteal flap from the olecranon",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "2",
                              "children": []
                            },
                            {
                              "text": "intraosseous suture anchors",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "2",
                              "children": []
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "avulsion",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "tension-band construct",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "screw and washer",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "post-op",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "immobilization in 30-45 degrees of flexion for 2 weeks",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "active ROM initiated at 4 weeks",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "avoid weightlifting for 4-6 months",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "complications specific to this treatment",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "olecranon bursitis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
